  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Via the defender – one-touch pass, shot and rebound",
  "description": "Three lines and a goalkeeper. A stands in the corner beside the goal, B along the same boards out at the defender position and C on the far side level with B. A passes along the boards to B and runs straight to the goal. B plays a one-touch pass across to C, who shoots first time. A is at the goal by then and looks for the rebound.\n\nRotation: A goes to B, B to C and C to A. Run it from both sides.\n\nEasier version: only A and B. A passes B along the boards, runs into the slot and gets a one-touch return that A shoots first time. Harder version: C chooses between shooting and passing to A in front of the goal. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Passes along the floor without bounces – vary forehand and backhand."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: run right after the pass and have the stick on the floor at the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "C: shoot first time and hit the target – a rebound needs a shot on goal."
    }
  ],
